        {"clause_id": "C23", "origin": "explicit", "interpretation": "Preserve the exclusion ID, role and required flag."},
        {"clause_id": "C29", "origin": "explicit", "interpretation": "Preserved N1 exclusion identity."}
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "O1",
      "revision": 1,
      "kind": "postcondition",
      "role": "guarantee",
      "required": true,
      "statement": "For every input satisfying A1, actual execution of the arity-1 typed entry solve in canonical program.vscore.json returns the exact integer sum Σ_{i=0}^{n-1} floor((a*i+b)/m). For each summand, floor is the unique integer q satisfying q*m <= a*i+b < (q+1)*m, including negative numerators. The empty sum for n=0 is zero. The formal contract must universally refine actual source execution to this complete formula and must also bind program.vscore.json, solve, arity 1 and typed_total, deterministic, input_preserved, no_external_io, no_floating_point, pure_data and restricted_runtime_only under normative Lean vscore-semantics/0.3 and data-pipeline/0.3. O1 is a mixed source/value guarantee with value_required=true.",
      "scope": ["all inputs satisfying A1", "actual canonical solve source and execution"],
      "dependencies": [
        {"id": "D1", "relation": "uses_definition"},
        {"id": "A1", "relation": "assumes"}
      ],
      "acceptance_criteria": [
        "For every valid integer input, actual solve execution returns Σ_{i=0}^{n-1} floor((a*i+b)/m).",
        "Each quotient satisfies q*m <= a*i+b < (q+1)*m; negative numerators use floor toward negative infinity.",
        "Every input with n=0 returns zero.",
        "solve({a:-2,b:1,m:3,n:4}) returns -4 and solve({a:100,b:-99,m:7,n:0}) returns 0.",
        "The formal contract includes canonical file program.vscore.json, entry solve, arity 1 and all seven closed source properties.",
        "Universal source implementation refinement and the complete functional formula are required; examples, result existence and substitute equalities cannot replace them."
      ],
